From: Princechudasama <chudasamaprince123@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:43:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replace in-memory movie storage with PostgreSQL + pgvector
 and Flyway

- Store movies and their Ollama embeddings in PostgreSQL (vector(768)) instead
  of an in-memory list; similarity search now runs in the database using
  pgvector's cosine distance operator and an HNSW index.
- Add Flyway migrations: enable pgvector, create movies table, create index.
- Add MovieRepository (JdbcTemplate), MovieSearchService and an idempotent
  MovieSeeder that embeds only movies missing from the database on startup.
- Slim OllamaEmbeddingService down to embedding generation and validate the
  returned dimension against the column size.
- Remove the unused in-memory MovieEmbedding model.
- Add docker-compose.yml (pgvector/pgvector:pg17), configuration properties,
  README instructions and unit tests for the vector literal helper.
- The REST API (POST /api/embeddings) request and response are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
